{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790979777,"nonce":"EcOlMLOK6AbrFaiJdo2Y5Iby6TM=","message":"Landed on branch `worktree-agent-a0efe8b2d2c617aa8` as `tui: expand is a layer spec, the fold arrow is a cell, nesting opens folded (f4426ff)`.\n\n**The spec, as parsed** (`view/expand.go`, checked in `view.Parse` and then against the schema in `view.CheckSchema`): `expand` is a string or an object. A string is the shorthand for one layer with every default, except `\"self\"`, which is refused at the top because it repeats the layer it is on and there is none. A layer takes `relation` (required), `query`, `fields`, `details`, `group_by`, `rank` and `expand`; any other key is refused naming the seven, and the error says which layer (`layer 2 takes no key depth`). `Layer.Layers()` flattens the chain into one layer per level and a `repeat` flag for a trailing `\"self\"`, so the renderer reads a row's layer off its level and never walks the spec. `depth` is gone from the table, so `{\"depth\":2}` is now refused as an unknown argument.\n\n**Inheritance**: `fields`, `details` and `rank` a layer does not name are the layer above's — so the bare `\"expand\":\"children\"` is exactly the old uniform tree, and the root's `rank` (already defaulted to the built-in `rank` by `rankArg`) flows down. `group_by` is *not* inherited: a level is sectioned because that level asked to be. A layer's `query` runs over the array of that row's own unarchived children, through `jq.Program.Run`, memoized per (layer, row); a query that fails or returns something that is not an issue puts its error on the status line and leaves that row's children unnarrowed, rather than emptying the tree.\n\n**The header follows the layer**: `listPage.columns()` is the fields of the layer the *cursor's row* is on, and `body()` draws the header from it; `widths()` sizes one set of columns per layer, measured over that layer's own rows, and `rowLine` draws each row with its own layer's fields and widths. So Tab/S-Tab, ↑/↓ and a refresh that lands the cursor elsewhere all change the header. A layer's `group_by` draws its own headers at the level's indent (`groupHeads`), and the sticky header machinery still tracks the roots' sections.\n\n**`self`**: implemented as a repeat of the layer it sits on, so `{\"relation\":\"children\",\"expand\":\"self\"}` is the old `depth: 0` — every level draws that layer's columns and runs its query, and cycles are cut at the repeat as before. `Z` on such a tree opens it all the way down.\n\n**The arrow cell**: the id column is first and flush again; the tree cell follows it with the level's indent, `▾`/`▸`, and the folded count — the row's own children, which is what unfolding reveals. `→` reaches it, `Space` folds (a leaf rings, `nothing to fold`), `Enter` opens the row as on the id. On the gantt it is the cell `←` reaches from the first period (`col == -1`), confirmed as you suggested; the crosshair is simply absent while the cursor is there, and a fold leaves the cursor on the arrow rather than snapping back into the chart. `z` is gone from `keys.go`, the help row and the hints; `Z` (`foldAll`) folds every parent where any is open and opens every one where none is.\n\n**Folded on open**: `nest` takes an `open` set rather than a `folded` one, so every parent starts shut and what is remembered across a refresh is what was opened. `reveal` opens a row's ancestors when a rebuild would leave the cursor's row hidden.\n\n**Calls beyond the brief, for the record:**\n- A layer's `group_by` draws real section headers under the parent, indented to the level, and a grab stays inside its section (`siblingAt`); only a root crosses groups, as before. The alternative was to accept `group_by` and only reorder by it, which would have been half a feature.\n- `overview` got `expand={\"relation\":\"children\"}` with defaults, exactly as decided, so a story's arrow counts *every* unarchived child, closed ones included; narrowing it to open tasks is one `query` on the layer if the count reads wrong in use.\n- The overdue/band work for `04248c5` is a separate commit.\n\n`gofmt`, `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` pass. `./gw flow import flows/` re-imported `overview` into the tracker.","files":null}]}